<title>USA: Interstate Hotels buys Florida resort for $47 mln.</title>
<headline>Interstate Hotels buys Florida resort for $47 mln.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH, Pa. 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interstate Hotels Co said Thursday that it has acquired the Indian River Plantation Resort on Hutchinson Island, Fla., for about $47 million from Radnor Corp.</p>
<p>The resort has 297 rooms and is located on 200 acres of oceanfront land 45 minutes north of Palm Beach International Airport.</p>
<p>Interstate is an independent hotel management company. With the addition of the Indian River property it will own or have a controlling interest in 30 hotels.</p>
</text>
